# Two menus for a fridge, chosen with a lever: on, cooked food only; off, field
# rations and mush bars. A change drops what the fridge no longer takes.
# d0: a fridge or a bin. d1: a switch (an IC Switch or a signal switch).
# Each item kind is one number put into the fridge's memory, the IC Sorter's
# "this item kind" filter: hash << 8 | SorterInstruction.FilterPrefabHashEquals.
# The checklist is set once the program yields, so it changes in one go.
alias fridge d0
alias lever d1
move r9 -1         # the lever as last seen; -1 so the first pass writes
start:
yield
l r0 lever Setting
beq r0 r9 start    # write only when the lever moves
move r9 r0
clr fridge
move r2 0          # next cell
beqz r0 plain
move r1 HASH("CookedMeat")
jal add
move r1 HASH("FriedMushBar")
jal add
j start
plain:
move r1 HASH("FieldRation")
jal add
move r1 HASH("MushBar")
jal add
j start
add:
sll r1 r1 8
or r1 r1 SorterInstruction.FilterPrefabHashEquals
put fridge r2 r1
add r2 r2 1
j ra
